Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:47:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Fix GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (CVE-2026-129292): FPM status
 page XSS via method, URI, user and script

The full FPM status page printed the request method, request URI, auth
user and script filename raw in every format; the query string was only
"escaped" for html/xml, with flags ENT_HTML_IGNORE_ERRORS & ENT_COMPAT
(= 0, so no quote escaping), and the JSON output was never escaped.
Escape all client-influenced fields through one helper.

Backport of php-src 37abd0a7f7 for EOL 7.4.33. 7.4 never got the earlier
GHSA-7qg2-v9fj-4mwv request-URI fix, so this covers it too. Differences:
- html/xml: php_escape_html_entities_ex() with the 7.4 signature (no
  quiet arg) and ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE | ENT_DISALLOWED |
  ENT_HTML_DOC_XML1 (upstream: ENT_COMPAT without ENT_SUBSTITUTE), so
  single quotes are escaped and invalid UTF-8 becomes U+FFFD instead of
  an empty string
- json: 7.4 has no php_json_encode_string() and ext/json can be built
  out, so a small static escaper is used: '"', '\\', '/' backslashed,
  control chars < 0x20 as \u00XX, invalid UTF-8 dropped (same as
  PHP_JSON_INVALID_UTF8_IGNORE upstream)
- a separate encode_json flag next to the existing encode (html/xml) one
- temporaries freed with zend_string_release_ex() (safe for interned
  strings) instead of zend_string_free()
- text/plain output unchanged
- test: 7.4's FPM tester has no multiRequest 'delay', so the busy request
  is sent with the raw FastCGI client and the status pages are fetched
  afterwards; also covers query string and xml output and checks that
  the JSON decodes

