From 2a14241e716488717e86f8ba370cc96a1da29675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:53:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Fix GHSA-fm2m-fjf5-v3cp (CVE-2026-126714): RCE via
 corrupted session file

ps_files_write() only truncated the session file when the new data was
shorter than the old, so an interrupted write could leave two partial
sessions concatenated in one file, whose serialized data an attacker may
be able to shape. Always truncate before writing and fail the write if
ftruncate() fails.

Backport of php-src e2d3cee9ad for EOL 7.4.33. The change is identical
(7.4's ps_files_write() returns int instead of zend_result; the
FAILURE return value is the same). Upstream has no test for this.
data->st_size is still maintained by ps_files_read() but no longer read
here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/session/mod_files.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/session/mod_files.c b/ext/session/mod_files.c
index cb8138e6..b9f5427e 100644
--- a/ext/session/mod_files.c
+++ b/ext/session/mod_files.c
@@ -240,9 +240,9 @@ static int ps_files_write(ps_files *data, zend_string *key, zend_string *val)
 		return FAILURE;
 	}
 
-	/* Truncate file if the amount of new data is smaller than the existing data set. */
-	if (ZSTR_LEN(val) < data->st_size) {
-		php_ignore_value(ftruncate(data->fd, 0));
+	if (ftruncate(data->fd, 0) != 0) {
+		php_error_docref(NULL, E_WARNING, "ftruncate() failed: %s (%d)", strerror(errno), errno);
+		return FAILURE;
 	}
 
 #if defined(HAVE_PWRITE)
From fab1c35b20c547d2dfc0d97a0a700b7fab75a8a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:54:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Fix GHSA-68fq-fh7h-f8gr (CVE-2026-128090): refuse
 keyless phar signature when .pubkey exists

The signature type is not covered by the signature itself, so an
OpenSSL-signed phar (phar, tar or zip format) could be downgraded to a
keyless hash (MD5/SHA*) computed by the attacker. Refuse any non-OpenSSL
signature when "<archive>.pubkey" exists.

Backport of php-src db90b7ba0d for EOL 7.4.33. Differences for 7.4:
- 7.4 only has PHAR_SIG_OPENSSL (no PHAR_SIG_OPENSSL_SHA256/_SHA512), so
  the check is sig_type != PHAR_SIG_OPENSSL
- zend_bool instead of bool
The test is taken unchanged (it already uses only 7.4 syntax; the
error-message formats in 7.4's phar.c/tar.c/zip.c match 8.2's).
Behaviour change: a non-OpenSSL-signed phar that has a stray .pubkey
file next to it no longer opens.

